REFERENCE · NIXOS GARBAGE COLLECTION
Deleting Old Generations

How to remove old system generations by number, free disk space, and refresh
the boot menu — without touching the generations you want to keep.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1 · List generations                                          (nothing deleted)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  sudo nix-env --list-generations -p /nix/var/nix/profiles/system

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 · Delete by generation number                         (keeps the rest intact)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Say the numbers run 81 to 90, with 90 current. To delete the oldest five:

  sudo nix-env --delete-generations 81 82 83 84 85 \
    -p /nix/var/nix/profiles/system

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3 · Free disk space and refresh the boot menu
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  sudo nix-collect-garbage
  sudo nixos-rebuild boot --flake /etc/nixos#nixos

Rebuilding is what actually removes the deleted entries from the
systemd-boot menu.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WARNING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Don't use nix-collect-garbage -d — it deletes *all* old generations, not
just the ones picked above.
